      <div type="clause" n="3.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 3.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Heafodmynstres<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.19"/> griðbryce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.20"/> is æt botwyrþum þingu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> be cingces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.21"/> munde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is mid V<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.22"/> pundum on Engla lage (⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.star3"/> on Centlande æt þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> mundbryce V pund þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cingce ⁊ þreo þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> arceb<hi rend="italic">iscope</hi>), ⁊ medemran mynstres mid CXX scill', <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.23"/>þæt is be cingces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.21"/> wite, ⁊ þonne gyt læssan, þær lytel þeowdom sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.11"/>, ⁊ legerstow þeah<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.24"/> sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.11"/>, mid LX scill', and feldcyricean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.25"/>, þær legerstow ne sig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.11"/>, mid XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.26"/> scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Heafodmynstres griðbrice is æt botwyrðum þyngum be cyninges munde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is mid fif pundum on Engla lage, and medemran mynstres mid an hundred ⁊ twentigum scyllingum — ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.3"/> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is be cyninges wite — and þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> gyt læssan, þær litel þeowdom sy, ⁊ legerstow þeah sy, mid sixtigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scill.', and feldcyrice, þær legerstow ne sy, mid ðrittigu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scyll.'</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="282" ed="#liebermann"/>Capitalis ęcclesię griðbreche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.2"/> (pacis fractio) in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.11-2"/> rebus emendabilibus est sicut infractio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.12"/> regię pacis, id est V libris in Anglorum lege, mediocris ęcclesię CXX solidis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.13"/>, id est wita regis, et adhuc minoris, ubi parva ecclesia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.2"/> est (parrochia sit) et atrium tamen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.14"/> sit, LX solidis, et campestris ęcclesię, ubi non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.15"/> sit atrium, XXX solidis.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Principales autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.30"/> ęcclesię, sicut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.31"/> episcopatus (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.32"/> abbatię), talem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.33"/> emendationem uiolatę pacis secundum legem Anglorum habere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.34"/> debent: mundam regis, hoc est quinque libras; secundum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.35"/> certe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.36"/> legem Danorum octo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.37"/> libras. | <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi> Mediocres autem ecclesie, ut abatie et canonicatus, iuxta forisfacturam regis, uidelicet XXC solidos, hoc est qaatuor libras. Minores quidem ecclesie, hoc est ubi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.38"/> seruitium fit, et tamen cimiterium habent, LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.39"/> solidos hoc est tres libras. Minime uero ecclesie, quam Angli feldcherche dicunt, id est carentes cimiterio, XXX sol. | <hi rend="italic">H Di Lb S Ct Jo</hi> Mediocris autem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.40"/> ęcclesię duas libras, hoc est secundum forisfacturam regis, et adhuc minoris ęcclesię, hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.41"/> est ubi parum seruitii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.42"/> fit, et tamen cimiterium habet, forisfactura est unius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.43"/> libre; minimę uero<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.44"/> ęcclesię, quam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.45"/> Angli feldcirice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="46" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.46"/> uocant, octoginta denariorum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="47" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.oe.47"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Matris ergo ecclesie pacis infracture emenda est iuxta montam regis, scilicet V libre in lege Anglorum; mediocris uero iuxta forisfacturam regis, uidelicet CXX solidi; agrestis autem ecclesie carentis cimiterio XXX solidi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="3a.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="156" ed="#robertson"/>Heafodmynstres<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.fn.9"/> griðbryce is æt botwyrþum þingum be cingces munde, þæt is mid V pundum on Engla lage, (⁊ on Centlande æt þam mundbryce V pund þam cingce ⁊ þreo þam arcebiscope)<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.fn.1"/>, ⁊ medemran mynstres mid CXX scill', þæt is be cingces wite, ⁊ þonne gyt læssan þær lytel þeowdom sig ⁊ legerstow þeah sig, mid LX scill', and feldcyricean þær legerstow ne sig mid XXX scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="234" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Heafodmynstres griðbryce is æt botwyrþum þingum be cingces munde, þæt is mid V pundum on Engla lage—and on Centlande æt þam mundbryce V pund þam cingce and þreo þam arcebiscope—and medemran mynstres mid CXX scillingum, þæt is be cingces wite, and þonne gyt læssan, þær lytel þeowdom sig, and legerstow þeah sig, mid LX scillingum, and feldcyricean, þær legerstow ne sig, mid XXX scyllinga.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="283" ed="#liebermann"/>Der Bruch des Sonderfriedens<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.1"/> einer Hauptkirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.2"/> bei bussfähigen Sachen geht nach dem [Betrag des] königlichen Sonderschutzes, nämlich mit fünf Pfund [Silber] nach Engländer-Recht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.3"/> (und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.4"/> in Kent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.5"/> [gehören] von diesem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.6"/> Bruche des Sonderschutzes fünf Pfund dem König und drei dem Erzbischofe <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) und der einer mittleren Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.7"/> mit 120<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.8"/> Schill., d. h. mit Königs-Strafgeld, und ferner der einer noch kleineren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.9"/>, wo wenig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.10"/> Gottesdienst ist und doch ein Friedhof zugehört, mit 60 Schill. und der einer Kirche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.11"/> auf dem [unbewohnten] Lande, wo kein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.12"/> Friedhof liegt, mit 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_3-2.lnote.de.13"/> Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Breach of the protection of a head minster in cases that can be compensated goes at [the amount of] the king's protection, that is with five pounds [of silver] under English law (and in Kent, for this breach of protection, five pounds [go] to the king and three to the archbishop, G); and of a middling minster with 120 shillings, that is at the king's fine; and of a still smaller one, where there is little divine service but there is a graveyard, with 60 shillings; and of a field-church, where there is no graveyard, with 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="157" ed="#robertson"/>Amends for violation of the protection of a principal church<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.n.1"/>, in cases in which compensation can be paid, shall be made by payment of the fine for breach of the king’s <hi rend="italic">mund</hi>, <hi rend="italic">i.e</hi>. £5 in districts under English law, (and in Kent<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.n.2"/> for breach of the <hi rend="italic">mund</hi>, £5 to the king and £3<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.n.3"/> to the Archbishop), and in the case of a church of medium rank<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#ICn_3-2.robnote.n.4"/>, by the payment of 120 shillings, <hi rend="italic">i.e</hi>. by the fine due to the king (for insubordination), and in the case of one still smaller where there is little divine service but where, however, there is a graveyard, by the payment of 60 shillings, and in the case of a country chapel where there is no graveyard, by the payment of 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="235" ed="#rabin-doml"/>The penalty for a sanctuary violation at a cathedral, when the violation is deemed eligible for compensation, is to be equal to that paid for a violation of the king’s protection, that is, five pounds under English law—and in Kent for a violation of protection, five pounds to the king and three to the archbishop—and at a midlevel church, one hundred twenty shillings, that is, equivalent to the penalty paid for an offense to the king; and at one yet smaller, where there is little divine service but there is a graveyard, sixty shillings; and at a country church where there is no graveyard, thirty shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="283"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_5">VIII Atr 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 5,</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_1-1">Leis Wl 1.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_2">Leis Wl 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>values recur</label> <ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref> <quote>But the values in Af 3 do recur in the 'G' MS of Wulfstan's I Cn 3:2, II 62.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="39"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_5-1">VIII Atr 5.1</ref> <quote>In VIII Atr 5:1 = I Cn 3:2, he reprised Edgar's distinction between 'headminsters', 'lesser' churches with a cemetery and 'field-churches'.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#rabin-doml" n="423"><label>contrasts with the equivalent clause</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_6">Grið 6</ref> <quote>The higher amount granted to the king in this clause contrasts with the equivalent clause in On Sanctuary</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="152"><ref target="clause:Af_3">Af 3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="336"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_5-1">VIII Atr 5.1</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">The Kentish addition in brackets is only in G (compare II Cn 62). A's ‘⁊’ before ‘þæt is be cyninges wite’ should be struck. The Instituta Cnuti add the Danish-law amount (8 pounds) and differ in detail. Liebermann compares VIII Atr 5.1.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 283, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">and on . . . arcebiscope: omitted A</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">five pounds: The higher amount granted to the king in this clause contrasts with the equivalent clause in On Sanctuary, which specifies that “in the laws of the Kentish people, the king and archbishop are owed an equal and likewise costly penalty for the violation of their protection” (clause 6).</note>
