        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">griðbrycc</hi> auch Hn 79, 6 hierher</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">griðbrycc</hi> also Hn 79, 6 belongs here</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Schreiber von Inst schwanken—schon vor 1150—, ob Abteien zum ersten Range der Kathedralen gehören; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The scribes of Inst waver — already before 1150 — as to whether abbeys belong to the first rank, that of the cathedrals; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst setzt hinzu: ‘in Dena lagu 8 £’, d. i. ‘hundert’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6) Silbers: also ebensoviel wie nach Hs. G in Kent</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst adds: ‘in Dena lagu 8 £’, i.e. a ‘hundred’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6) of silver: thus as much as in Kent according to MS G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">G zeigt Zusätze für Canterbury; <hi rend="italic">s. o</hi>. Einl. 7</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">G shows additions for Canterbury; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Introduction 7</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ebenso Grið 11, dagegen (nach Kenter Gesetz 7. Jhs.) 6: <hi rend="italic">on Cantwara lage cyning ⁊ arcebiscop gelicne mundbryce</hi>; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Kent 8a; b; Erzbischof 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Likewise Grið 11, whereas (following the Kentish law of the 7th cent.) 6 has: <hi rend="italic">on Cantwara lage cyning ⁊ arcebiscop gelicne mundbryce</hi>; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Kent 8a; b; Erzbischof 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘bei dem Bruch des Mundiums’ allgemein [Schmid], sondern nur dieses in Z. 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘in the case of breach of the mund’ in general [Schmid], but only of this one in l. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zu Inst <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Kanoniker 1b. Kanonikerstifte Lothringischen Musters entstanden in England erst nach Cnut</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On Inst <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Kanoniker 1b. Houses of canons on the Lotharingian model arose in England only after Cnut</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hn rechnet richtig Normannisch zu 50 Schill. um. In Inst meint eine Hss.-Klasse irrig, Cnut rechne nach Merc. Schilling von ¹/₆₀ £. Cb scheint <hi rend="italic">XXC</hi> aus <hi rend="italic">CXX</hi> zu verlesen und als Norm. Schill. von ¹/₂₀ £ misszuverstehen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hn correctly converts this into Norman reckoning as 50 shill. In Inst one class of MSS wrongly supposes that Cnut reckons in Mercian shillings of ¹/₆₀ £. Cb seems to misread <hi rend="italic">CXX</hi> as <hi rend="italic">XXC</hi> and to misunderstand it as Norman shill. of ¹/₂₀ £</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese Klasse fehlt Cons.—Die beiden Inst-Klassen irren in der Umrechnung wie in vor. Erkl.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cons lacks this class. — The two classes of Inst err in the conversion as in the preceding note</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Kirchenrang 3c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.11" n="11" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Kapelle’ Hn; statt ‘unbewohnten’ setze deutlicher ‘offenen’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘chapel’ Hn; instead of ‘unbewohnten’ (‘uninhabited’) put, more clearly, ‘offenen’ (‘open’)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.12" n="12" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wohl blosse Verdeutlichung zu Atr</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Probably a mere clarification added to Atr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.13" n="13" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">199</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Vielleicht verschrieb Inst-Klasse 2 <hi rend="italic">XXC</hi>, wie <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. Erkl. 8 (statt <hi rend="italic">CXX</hi>), was richtig wäre für die [irrige] Annahme, Cnut rechne nach Merc. Schilling</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Perhaps Inst class 2 miswrote <hi rend="italic">XXC</hi>, as <hi rend="italic">above</hi> note 8 (instead of <hi rend="italic">CXX</hi>), which would be correct on the [mistaken] assumption that Cnut reckons in Mercian shillings</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_3-2.lnote.de.0" n="0" source="#liebermann-erkl" rend="wholeClause"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">198</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Am Rande lies ‘5, 1’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In the margin read ‘5, 1’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">principales ecclesiae sicut episcopatus et abbatiae</hi> is the reading of Inst. except in one MS which classes <hi rend="italic">abbatiae</hi> along with <hi rend="italic">canonicatus</hi> as <hi rend="italic">mediocres ecclesiae</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause, which is an addition in G, cf. <hi rend="italic">Be Griðe</hi>, 11 (drawn from Af. 3), and note the discrepancy between it and cap. 6: <hi rend="italic">on Cantwara lage cyning ⁊ arcebiscop agan gelicne and efen dyrne mundbryce</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. Af. 3; II Cn. 58, 1; 62 G. Inst. adds: <hi rend="italic">secundum certe legem Danorum octo libras</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.n.4" n="4" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">348</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that collegiate foundations are probably meant, cf. <hi rend="italic">canonicatus</hi>, Inst.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>sig</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">is</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_3-2.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><label>Heafodmynstres</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">heafodcyricum</hi> Ld.</seg></note>
